Phillip Helbig---undress to reply wrote:

> I have a few cables which are Centronics 50 at one end and, at least
> physically, a FEMALE HD68 at the other end.  I suspect that this is the
> cable for the strange SCSI on a VAXstation 3100 (which has a MALE socket
> on the VAXstation, which physically looks like an HD68 cable).
> 
> Is there anything else this could be?
> 
> If I connect this to a normal HD68 cable, will this work to connect a
> Centronics 50 device to an HD68 SCSI connector on a computer or vice
> versa?

No, definitely those cables are not usable for HD68 (wide) SCSI.
The Vaxstation 3100 interface is SCSI-1 or SCSI-2, and the connector was 
used long before the wide SCSI with HD68 connectors appeared.
Happily they have the wrong "sex", so one doesn't easily take it on real 
SCSI-3 wide interfaces.
And no, they not necessarily have D.I.G.I.T.A.L brand, I had a lot of them 
from Inmac and other sources.

