RRD46 drives are now long in the tooth, dating from the time when CD 
buring was in its infancy.  I think I would avoid CD-RWs with them. 
CD-RWs have always had the reputation for being pretty flaky, so I never 
use them for anything important.

Try burning a CD-R at a really slow burn rate like 4x, using a good 
quality blank CD-R, and try the resulting coaster.

Is there the possibility that your Alpha might accept as one of its own 
a newer SCSI CD-RW drive, like a Plextor?

... Ben Myers


